course: dictionary
lesson: 13629
title: Indivisible: cannot be split
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indivisible is made of «in-», meaning not, and «divisible», meaning able to be divided. So indivisible means not able to be split into parts. Look at the parts of a word to help you guess its meaning.
explain: In maths, indivisible means a number cannot be shared out exactly. «Seven is indivisible by two.» If you share seven into two equal groups, one is left over, so it does not divide exactly.
explain: Some people use the word for a whole that must stay together. «Our class said the Pledge of Allegiance: one nation, indivisible.» The country is one whole and should not be broken up.
fact: Indivisible means not able to be divided or separated into parts.
fact: «Nine is indivisible by four» means four does not go into nine exactly; there is a remainder of one.
fact: A prime number is indivisible by any number except 1 and itself.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «indivisible by» and «one and indivisible».
fact: In science, atoms were once thought to be indivisible, but scientists later found that they could be split.
exercise: «Seven is indivisible by two.» What does this tell you? | *It leaves a remainder when shared into two equal groups | Seven can be shared into two equal groups with none left over | Two is bigger than seven | It is an even number
exercise: What does indivisible mean? | Able to be shared out equally | Very large | *Not able to be split into parts | Broken into many small pieces
exercise: «One nation, indivisible.» What does indivisible suggest here? | *Closely joined so they act as one | Old-fashioned | Tiny | Divided into groups
test: «Nine is indivisible by four.» Is there a remainder when nine is divided by four? | No, four is bigger than nine | Yes, there is a remainder of four | *Yes, there is a remainder of one | No, nine divides by four exactly
test: Which number is a prime number, so it is indivisible by any number except 1 and itself? | Six | *Seven | Nine | Four
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The atom was once thought to be indivisible»? | *It could not be split into smaller parts, people thought | It was easy to break apart | It was very small and light | It was always moving around
